# direnv config — auto-loads .env into the shell when you cd into this
# directory. Required for:
#   - The Neon MCP server (reads NEON_API_KEY from the env)
#   - Any ad-hoc `pnpm rando ...` invocation outside the `rando` shebang
#     wrapper (which loads .env via --env-file-if-exists for its own
#     subprocess — direnv covers the rest)
#
# .env is gitignored; this file is committed so every dev gets the
# same auto-load behavior after running `direnv allow`.
#
# Setup is one-time per dev: see .github/CONTRIBUTING.md → "Shell env
# via direnv (optional but recommended)" for the hook + `direnv allow`
# step. `./scripts/bootstrap` runs `direnv allow` automatically.

dotenv_if_exists .env
